Modifications (marked as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):
  The files in this directory (`code/life/`) reimplement the *structure* and the
  prompt organization of the Generative Agents cognitive architecture for our
  deterministic, event-log-anchored world. They are substantially modified:

    agent.py     adapted from  persona/persona.py  (Persona.move main loop:
                   perceive -> retrieve -> plan -> act -> reflect)
    memory.py    adapted from  persona/memory_structures/associative_memory.py
                   and persona/cognitive_modules/{retrieve,reflect}.py
                   (memory stream + three-factor retrieval + reflection trigger)
    plan.py/plan logic adapted from persona/cognitive_modules/plan.py (template)

  Key changes vs. the original:
    * every step reads ONLY from the kernel's IF-1 `perceive()` and writes ONLY
      via IF-2 `submit_intent()` — the agent never mutates world state;
    * all LLM output is routed through a freezable `LLMClient` and is not used to
      decide world randomness (RNG decides branches; the LLM only fills content);
    * memory bodies/embeddings are stored in side storage; the ledger stores only
      references; retrieval hits are logged so replay never recomputes embeddings.
